ke  the action that was needed according to  environmentalists  living on the front line mia motley is  the prime minister of barbados a small  island nation that was battered by a  hurricane in july cold red  cold red  to the g7 countries  code red  code red to the g20  earth the cop  that's what it said  earth to cop  for those who have ice to see for those  who have ears to listen  and for those who have a heart to feel  1.5 is what we need to survive the  urgency of the situation is obvious but  it's still not clear there's the  commitment by all nations to try to fix  things  james bays al jazeera glasgow  well our environment editor nick clark  continues our cop 26 coverage live from  glasgow nick  hello yeah thanks very much lots of bold  impassioned speeches on day two of the  u.n climate conference here in glasgow  but then  u.n prime minister narendra modi  came to the stage came to the podium and  just before we go to a clip of his  remember that a key target here is to  get all the countries to agree that net  zero should happen by 2050.  he really  changed direction on that and said that  he's going for 2017.  india will fulfill 50 of its energy  requirements from renewable energy  sources by 2030 between now and 2030  india will reduce its total projected  carbon emissions by 1 billion tons by  2030 india will reduce the carbon  intensity of its economy by 45  and by 2070 india will achieve the  target of net zero emissions  well let's explore this further take  this on we can speak to uh peter betts  uh he's an associate fellow in the  energy and environment resources program  at chatham house and you were also a  former lead negotiator with the eu in  the uk so you know exactly what's what  at these climate conferences so first up  the indian pm just going for net zero by  2070. they hadn't actually come up with  any pledge to for carbon neutral at any  point but now they have but it's 2070  which is 20 years two decades after the  target here which 